---
title: "{js} cell error state"
---

A `{js}` cell that throws at runtime surfaces the `.tmd-js-error` box. The box is
themed for **light and dark** (the dark override lives in `dark.css`), so this doc
pins that runtime-error state as a target for browser verification. The corpus
render only emits the cell (JS runs in the browser, not at build time), so this
doc renders without warnings like any other.

```{js}
throw new Error("intentional: pins the .tmd-js-error box for light + dark themes");
```

Prose after the failing cell still renders normally, confirming one cell's error
does not wedge the rest of the page.
